    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is headlined by the elite-tier production expected from **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (66.01) and **Coby Mayo** (66.72). **Coby Mayo** represents our most compelling start; despite facing the formidable McClanahan, the combined benefits of a favorable park factor (+16%) and his strong platoon edge (+8%) vault him to the top of our daily efficiency rankings. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a locked-in core play, leveraging a positive park adjustment to overcome a moderate SP skill disadvantage. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces the same tough southpaw, his elite raw talent keeps his output high (64.35), though we are tempering expectations slightly due to the negative platoon variance inherent in that matchup.\n\nBeyond our core, we are leaning into favorable platoon dynamics to maximize our daily floor. **Liam Hicks** (59.93) is a surprisingly strong play at C1 today, benefiting significantly from a weak SP_xERA of 4.52 and a massive park boost. We are monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (58.98) closely; although his raw projection is mitigated by his high-speed profile\u2014which often suffers against high-hold pitchers\u2014his dynamic platoon advantage against Kremer makes him a reliable start. Regarding our bench, **Heliot Ramos** (46.35) provided the most significant challenge to the current configuration. While he offered a slight edge in stolen base potential due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, the superior offensive efficiency and order placement of **Sam Antonacci** and **Luis Robert Jr.** ultimately dictated his exclusion to protect our games-played caps.\n\nCaution is advised regarding the bottom half of the lineup, as we are navigating a few matchups against high-end talent. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (54.95) remains in the lineup due to his reliable contact, he faces a difficult assignment in Cease. Furthermore, we are keeping a close eye on **Drake Baldwin** (46.61); his high-order position provides stability, but he is running into a buzzsaw in Henderson, whose 2.90 xERA creates a significant ceiling risk. We continue to hold **Andy Pages** and **Jacob Wilson** on the shelf as they recover from their respective injuries, ensuring we maintain roster flexibility while we navigate the final stretch of the 2026 season.",
